WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.960
Star Wars: The Last Jedi is one of the biggest
cinematic spectacles of the year. In addition

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:10.469
to returning characters like Luke, Rey, Finn,
and Kylo Ren, the eighth film in the Skywalker

00:00:10.469 --> 00:00:15.240
saga will add several new faces, like Kelly
Marie Tran, who's been referred to as the

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.080
"biggest new part" of The Last Jedi.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:21.960
In the film, she portrays Rose, a member of
the Resistance who works side-by-side with

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:22.460
Finn.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.180
Kelly Marie Tran might not be a household
name yet, but it won't be long before her

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:30.980
face is gracing thousands of action figures
and posters. Nonetheless, she might look awfully

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:35.660
familiar to Star Wars fans, and with good
reason. Here are just a few of the places

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.840
you may have seen her before.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:38.260
Web Shorts

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:44.260
Kelly Marie Tran grew up in San Diego, California,
and caught the acting bug early on. In high

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:49.250
school, she took to the stage, appearing in
plays, musicals and later, alongside improv

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:52.260
comedy troupes throughout her education at
UCLA.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.410
She eventually transitioned to doing digital
shorts and earned her first starring role

00:00:56.410 --> 00:01:01.880
as a cast member of the YouTube comedy series
Ladies Like Us. A meta-commentary of sorts,

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:05.700
the web saga followed the adventures of three
would-be up-and-comers from an all-female

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:11.180
comedy troupe. The series explored the challenges
of seeking out fame and fortune in the wannabe-saturated

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:16.270
world of Los Angeles. And each webisode also
explored or parodied standard character tropes

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:21.450
like personal insecurity, bad boyfriends,
and expectations foisted on women by Hollywood

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:22.080
and the media.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.720
Tran's quirky character charms the audience,
and the show's hip-hop-fueled vibe and crude

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.540
elements are reminiscent of the ladies from
Broad City.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:30.840
About a Boy

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:35.340
Tran next made her mark on the acting world
by landing a small role on the short-lived

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:41.150
NBC series About a Boy. Based on Nick Hornby's
novel, the show starred David Walton and Minnie

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:45.560
Driver. And although the series only lasted
for two seasons, it garnered a cult following

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:49.979
and above-average critical ratings. The one-camera
sitcom shadowed man-child singer-songwriter,

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:55.560
Will, as his awkward relationship with his
neighbors upset his otherwise libertine lifestyle.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:00.740
On the show, Tran popped in twice as Marguerite,
a thoroughly inattentive babysitter. It was

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:05.540
hardly the breakout role for the young actress,
but it did allow her to flex a few comedic

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:07.840
muscles on a major network-based sitcom.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.420
PSA days

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:14.819
As part of her foray into comedy, Tran also
starred in several madcap webisodes for College

00:02:14.819 --> 00:02:19.780
Humor, creating some memorably amusing sketches.
Among the wittiest clips was her role as a

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:24.011
member of a political correctness-monitoring
Asian council in "Are You Asian Enough?" She

00:02:24.011 --> 00:02:28.730
also dropped by a startup app developer i
n the poignant yet funny "Why Net Neutrality

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.580
Matters (and What You Can Do To Help)."

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.440
Of course, not all of her PSAs were quite
as hilarious as those. She also appeared in

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:40.010
one the anti-smoking Truth campaign ads -- and,
ironically enough, it's one that had a Star

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:40.940
Wars twist to it.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.310
"I only smoke when I …"

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:43.760
"Oh It's a trap!"

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.120
Pub Quiz

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:50.500
As Tran built her voice and her personal brand
on network TV, the burgeoning actress landed

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:55.740
roles on several web series, like Hope &amp; Randy—where
she played the roommate of the lead couple.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:03:01.300
In 2016, she wound up with a major role in
a full-length TV pilot about a band of rowdy

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:05.950
bar trivia junkies. Pub Quiz followed a gang
of screw-ups and their misadventures as they

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.740
sought to dominate the liquor-soaked bar quiz
world.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:13.500
These are all small potato projects, in comparison
to The Last Jedi, but, hey, everybody's gotta

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.500
start somewhere.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:19.120
Thanks for watching! Click the Looper icon
to subscribe to our YouTube channel. Plus

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.939
check out all this cool stuff we know you'll
love, too!

